# AI Server Patterns (apps/ai)

## Routes

Same structure as `crud` — one router per resource, `is_authenticated` first, export as `*_router`.

```ts
// src/routes/chat.ts
const router: IRouter = Router();
router.use(is_authenticated);
router.post("/:id/completion", chat_completion); // SSE — web
export { router as chat_router };
```

Mounted in `app.ts` at `/chats`, `/agents`, `/quiz`. Socket.IO is attached to the **same HTTP server** for mobile clients — both transports share the identical emitter pipeline.

---

## Streaming Architecture — Two Transports, One Pipeline

The service layer (`run_chat_completion`, `run_agent_loop`) is completely transport-agnostic. It receives an `emitters` object and calls its callbacks. The controller decides which transport fills those callbacks.

```
Client (web)  ──SSE──►  Express controller  ──emitters──►  run_chat_completion
Client (app)  ──WS───►  Socket.IO handler   ──emitters──►  run_chat_completion
                                                                  │
                                                         run_agent_loop
                                                         stream_text_with_fallback
```

### Emitter interface (shared)

```ts
// src/types/emitters.ts
export interface TStreamEmitters {
  on_validated: () => void;
  on_title: (title: string) => void;
  on_text_delta: (text: string) => void;
  on_thinking_delta: (text: string) => void;
  on_tool_call: (e: TToolCallEvent) => void;
  on_tool_result: (e: TToolResultEvent) => void;
  on_status: (text: string) => void;
  on_complete: (conversation_id: string) => void;
  on_error: (message: string) => void;
}
```

---

## Transport 1 — SSE (web / Next.js)

### Server: controller sets up SSE headers inside `on_validated`

```ts
// src/controllers/chat/chat-completion.ts
export const chat_completion = async (req: Request, res: Response) => {
  const { id: user_id } = req.user!;
  const { id: conversation_id } = z_chat_completion_params.parse(req.params);
  const { prompt, user_files } = z_chat_completion_body.parse(req.body);

  await run_chat_completion({
    conversation_id,
    user_id,
    prompt,
    user_files,
    emitters: {
      on_validated: () => {
        res.setHeader("Content-Type", "text/event-stream");
        res.setHeader("Cache-Control", "no-cache");
        res.setHeader("Connection", "keep-alive");
        res.flushHeaders();
      },
      on_title: (title) =>
        res.write(`event: title\ndata: ${JSON.stringify({ title })}\n\n`),
      on_text_delta: (text) =>
        res.write(`event: text-delta\ndata: ${JSON.stringify({ text })}\n\n`),
      on_thinking_delta: (text) =>
        res.write(
          `event: thinking-delta\ndata: ${JSON.stringify({ text })}\n\n`
        ),
      on_tool_call: (e) =>
        res.write(`event: tool-call\ndata: ${JSON.stringify(e)}\n\n`),
      on_tool_result: (e) =>
        res.write(`event: tool-result\ndata: ${JSON.stringify(e)}\n\n`),
      on_status: (text) =>
        res.write(`event: status\ndata: ${JSON.stringify({ text })}\n\n`),
      on_complete: (id) => {
        res.write(
          `event: complete\ndata: ${JSON.stringify({ conversation_id: id })}\n\n`
        );
        res.end();
      },
      on_error: (msg) => {
        res.write(
          `event: error\ndata: ${JSON.stringify({ message: msg })}\n\n`
        );
        res.end();
      },
    },
  });
};
```

**Rules:**

- SSE headers are **only** set inside `on_validated` — never before validation, never inside a service
- `on_validated` is called after the conversation is loaded and the user message is persisted — headers flush only when the request is confirmed valid
- `on_complete` and `on_error` both call `res.end()` — never leave the connection open after either

### Client: consuming SSE in Next.js (web)

Use the native `fetch` API with a `ReadableStream` decoder — **not** `EventSource` (EventSource cannot send POST bodies or custom headers).

```ts
// apps/web/src/hooks/use-chat-stream.ts
export function useChatStream() {
  const stream_completion = async (conversation_id: string, prompt: string) => {
    const token = await firebase_auth.currentUser?.getIdToken();

    const res = await fetch(
      `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_URL}/chats/${conversation_id}/completion`,
      {
        method: "POST",
        headers: {
          "Content-Type": "application/json",
          Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
        },
        body: JSON.stringify({ prompt }),
      }
    );

    if (!res.ok || !res.body) throw new Error("Stream failed");

    const reader = res.body.getReader();
    const decoder = new TextDecoder();
    let buffer = "";

    while (true) {
      const { done, value } = await reader.read();
      if (done) break;

      buffer += decoder.decode(value, { stream: true });
      const parts = buffer.split("\n\n");
      buffer = parts.pop() ?? ""; // keep incomplete trailing chunk

      for (const part of parts) {
        const event_line = part.match(/^event: (\S+)/);
        const data_line = part.match(/^data: (.+)/m);
        if (!event_line || !data_line) continue;

        const event = event_line[1];
        const data = JSON.parse(data_line[1]);

        switch (event) {
          case "title":
            handle_title(data.title);
            break;
          case "text-delta":
            handle_delta(data.text);
            break;
          case "thinking-delta":
            handle_thinking(data.text);
            break;
          case "tool-call":
            handle_tool_call(data);
            break;
          case "tool-result":
            handle_tool_result(data);
            break;
          case "status":
            handle_status(data.text);
            break;
          case "complete":
            handle_complete(data.conversation_id);
            break;
          case "error":
            handle_error(data.message);
            break;
        }
      }
    }
  };

  return { stream_completion };
}
```

